-- title:
--   At most two minimal primes over varpi in the j-finite chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M \neq 0$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of level $\{p\}$, with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,L$ applied to the function field $\mathrm{x1FunctionField}\,(Mp)$ of $X_1(Mp)$, i.e. the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the image of that field of $q$-expansions under the coefficientwise map $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,L$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j \in K$, $j \neq 0$, have Laurent series $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,L\,\mathrm{jq}$, the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Further data: an integer $d$ coprime to $Mp$, an $L$-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of $K$ agreeing, inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, with the base change to $L$ of the diamond automorphism $\langle d \rangle$ of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$, and a ring endomorphism $\rho$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ — the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$ — inducing $\theta$ on elements. Finally let $\mathfrak{P}_1$ be a minimal prime of the ideal of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ generated by the image of $\varpi$. The conclusion is that any two minimal primes $\mathfrak{P}, \mathfrak{P}'$ of that ideal with $\mathfrak{P} \neq \mathfrak{P}_1$ and $\mathfrak{P}' \neq \mathfrak{P}_1$ are equal; equivalently, the ideal has at most two minimal primes.
--
--   The statement expresses, in terms of the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model, that the fibre over the closed point of $A$ of the integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ has at most two irreducible components meeting that chart, the Gauss component and its twist; it is obtained from the classification of the valuation subrings of $K$ lying over the maximal ideal of $A$ and over the generic point of the $j$-line. It is used to show that the diamond automorphism $\langle d \rangle$ fixes each minimal prime over the uniformiser.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_eq_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span_of_ne_of_ne_chartAlgFin_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul.lean

